Package: patrone-branding
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         fonts-inter,
         fonts-noto-core,
         plymouth-theme-spinner,
         plymouth-theme-ubuntu-text
Description: Patrone Linux's name, logos and artwork
 Names the system Patrone Linux and puts Patrone's logo where Ubuntu's was:
 the boot splash, the boot menu, the login screen, Settings > About, the text
 console's banner and the welcome message at login, which also loses Ubuntu's
 help links, news and Ubuntu Pro advertising. The login screen gets Patrone's
 colors and a blue default avatar. Inter is the typeface everywhere: the
 desktop, apps, the login screen, and web pages that ask for Segoe UI or a
 plain sans-serif font, Chromium's included. It installs the
 Patrone wallpaper as the default, makes blue the accent color in place of
 Ubuntu's orange, turns Ubuntu's dock off by default, and sets up fastfetch
 with the Patrone logo. Removing the package puts Ubuntu's files back.
